menu "Wi-Fi Manager Configuration"

    config WIFI_STA_TIMEOUT_S
        int "STA connection timeout (seconds)"
        default 10

    config WIFI_MAX_RETRIES
        int "Max STA reconnect retries before AP fallback"
        default 5

    config WIFI_AP_STA_RETRY_S
        int "Retry stored credentials from AP mode every N seconds"
        default 30
        range 10 600
        help
            AP fallback is not a terminal state. While the provisioning AP is
            running, the stored NVS credentials are retried this often, so an
            outage longer than WIFI_MAX_RETRIES tolerates — a router reboot,
            for instance — recovers without a power cycle. Retries are skipped
            while a client is connected to the AP, so they never interrupt
            someone entering credentials.

    config WIFI_AP_SSID
        string "AP mode SSID"
        default "EDG-Setup"

    config WIFI_AP_PASSWORD
        string "AP mode password"
        default "edg12345"

    config WIFI_AP_CHANNEL
        int "AP mode channel"
        default 1
        range 1 13

    config WIFI_POWER_SAVE
        bool "Enable Wi-Fi modem power save (WIFI_PS_MIN_MODEM)"
        default n
        help
            ESP-IDF's own default is WIFI_PS_MIN_MODEM, which sleeps the radio
            between DTIM beacons and adds a latency tail measured at hundreds
            of milliseconds — enough to breach REQ-NF-004 (telemetry to
            browser within 500 ms) on this workload. The gateway is
            mains-powered, so this defaults to off. Turn it on for a
            battery-powered build where current draw matters more than
            telemetry latency.

    config WIFI_PROVISION_PORT
        int "Provisioning HTTP server port (AP mode)"
        default 8080
        help
            Separate from the telemetry dashboard's port (publisher's
            WS_SERVER_PORT, default 80) so both servers can run at once:
            WsPublisher's dashboard stays reachable at all times (sensors run
            regardless of Wi-Fi state), while this port serves the
            credential-entry form only while in AP mode.

endmenu
